Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Should Fail",
  "description": "This should return 403 if logged in as USER",
  "deadline": "2026-03-15T17:00:00",
  "durationHours": 8,
  "priorityId": 1,
  "statusId": 1
}

### ==================== SCHEDULING (main-backend → side-backend) ====================
### These endpoints trigger the full integration:
###   main-backend (8080) reads DB → sends to side-backend (8081) → algorithm runs → results saved to DB
### Requires: ADMIN role. Login first (see Authentication section above).

### Run scheduling with GREEDY strategy (best-fit by priority)
### Assigns tasks to the least-loaded eligible employee
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedule/run?strategy=GREEDY
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Run scheduling with ROUND_ROBIN strategy (fair distribution)
### Distributes tasks evenly across all eligible employees
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedule/run?strategy=ROUND_ROBIN
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ==================== SIDE-BACKEND DIRECT (port 8081) ====================
### These call the side-backend sandbox directly, bypassing main-backend.
### Useful for testing the algorithm in isolation with custom data.

@sideUrl = http://localhost:8081

### ✅ Happy path — GREEDY, 1 user, 1 task
POST {{sideUrl}}/api/v1/algo/schedule
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "strategy": "GREEDY",
  "users": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "firstName": "Alice",
      "lastName": "Smith",
      "email": "alice@example.com",
      "dailyAvailabilityHours": 8,
      "maxTasks": 5,
      "roles": ["WORKER"],
      "vacations": []
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Build Login Page",
      "description": "Create the login UI",
      "durationHours": 4,
      "deadline": "2026-12-31T23:59:59",
      "priority": "HIGH",
      "priorityLevel": 3,
      "status": "PENDING",
      "requiredRoles": ["WORKER"],
      "predecessorTaskIds": [],
      "successorTaskIds": []
    }
  ]
}

